Task 1: Backup Vault Data
Subtask 1.1: Install and Configure HashiCorp Vault
First, we need to install Vault and set up a basic configuration with sample data.

Step 1: Update the system and install required packages

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y wget unzip curl jq
Step 2: Download and install HashiCorp Vault

# Download Vault binary
wget https://releases.hashicorp.com/vault/1.15.2/vault_1.15.2_linux_amd64.zip

# Unzip the binary
unzip vault_1.15.2_linux_amd64.zip

# Move to system path
sudo mv vault /usr/local/bin/

# Verify installation
vault version
Step 3: Create Vault configuration directory and files

# Create Vault directory structure
sudo mkdir -p /opt/vault/data
sudo mkdir -p /opt/vault/config
sudo mkdir -p /opt/vault/logs
sudo mkdir -p /opt/vault/backups

# Create Vault configuration file
sudo tee /opt/vault/config/vault.hcl > /dev/null <<EOF
storage "file" {
  path = "/opt/vault/data"
}

listener "tcp" {
  address     = "127.0.0.1:8200"
  tls_disable = 1
}

api_addr = "http://127.0.0.1:8200"
cluster_addr = "https://127.0.0.1:8201"
ui = true
disable_mlock = true
EOF

# Set proper permissions
sudo chown -R $USER:$USER /opt/vault
